# Flyway Migration Conventions

Full reference: [flyway-migrations skill](../../.claude/skills/flyway-migrations/SKILL.md). This rule is the fast-path checklist — read the skill for annotated examples.

## Runner

`pnpm migrate` is the **only** way to apply migrations. TypeORM `migration:run` has been removed. Never call Flyway inside app startup code.

## Naming — `V<integer>__<snake_case>.sql`

Every file in `db/migrations/` must match this pattern exactly:

```
V10__add_shop_rating_column.sql   ✓
V10__AddShopRating.sql            ✗  camelCase in description
V1740000000000__init.sql          ✗  timestamp as version
V10.1__patch.sql                  ✗  decimal version
```

- Version is a plain incrementing integer — no gaps, no decimals, no timestamps
- Description uses `snake_case`; double underscore (`__`) is the separator
- `outOfOrder: false` in `flyway.config.js` — Flyway rejects out-of-sequence files

## Immutability

Once a migration file has been applied to **any** environment, its filename and SQL content are permanent. Flyway validates checksums on every `pnpm migrate` run — editing an applied file causes a checksum mismatch error.

**To fix a mistake in an applied migration: write a new `V<n+1>__fix_*.sql`.** Never edit the original.

## Destructive Changes — Always Two Steps

Flyway Community Edition has no rollback. `DROP COLUMN`, `DROP TABLE`, type narrowing, and constraint tightening on populated columns must span two separate releases:

1. **Release N** — add new structure, backfill data, stop writing to old column
2. **Release N+1** — drop the deprecated column/table after confirming zero usage

Never combine a `DROP` with feature work in the same migration.

## FK Index Requirement

Every `FOREIGN KEY` column must have a `CREATE INDEX` in the **same** migration file, unless a composite index already covers it as the leading column. Flag any FK without a matching index.

```sql
-- Required pattern
CONSTRAINT fk_orders_shop FOREIGN KEY (shop_id) REFERENCES shops (id) ON DELETE RESTRICT
...
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_shop ON orders (shop_id);   -- must be present
```

## Authoring Order Within a File

1. `CREATE EXTENSION` / `CREATE TYPE` (if needed)
2. `CREATE TABLE` (columns → PK → FK constraints → CHECK constraints)
3. `CREATE INDEX` statements (one per index, after the table)
4. `ALTER TABLE … ADD CONSTRAINT … EXCLUDE …` (after indexes)

## Money, Timestamps, Status Columns

- Money: `bigint` with `*_paise` suffix — never `numeric` or `float`
- Timestamps: `timestamptz` only — never bare `timestamp`
- Status enums: `CONSTRAINT chk_<table>_<col> CHECK (col IN (…))` — no Postgres `ENUM` type

## Verification Checklist (per migration)

- [ ] Version is next integer; no existing file has this version
- [ ] Filename: `V<n>__<snake_case>.sql`
- [ ] Every FK column has a `CREATE INDEX` in this file (or composite leading-column justification)
- [ ] Money columns: `bigint *_paise`
- [ ] Timestamps: `timestamptz`
- [ ] Status columns: CHECK constraint with exhaustive list
- [ ] `ON DELETE` explicit on every `FOREIGN KEY`
- [ ] Destructive change? Two-step plan spans two version numbers
- [ ] Runs cleanly: `pnpm migrate` → `pnpm migrate:info` shows Success
